    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered sequence of validations and side-effects applied when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`. The flow lives in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:110`), which implements the OpenAPI-generated `OwnersApi` interface.\n\n## Validations (in order)\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` requires `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`; otherwise 403/401.\n\n2. **Bean Validation on the request body** (`@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`), before the method body runs \u2014 failure \u2192 **400**:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 space/'/- separated words)\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, trailing `.` allowed)\n   - `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern` (non-blank)\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`, `@Pattern` (non-blank)\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`, `@Pattern` (`+`, digits, spaces, `()`, `-`)\n   - `email` \u2014 optional; `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`\n   - `postcode` \u2014 optional; `@Pattern(^\\d{4}$)`\n\n3. **Mapping-time validators/normalizers** (inside `ownerMapper.toOwner`, throwing `IllegalArgumentException` \u2192 **400**):\n   - `normalizeTelephone` \u2192 converts to E.164 (assumes `+61` when no `+`, drops national leading `0`), enforces 8\u201315 digits, then `E164NationalLength.check` (+61 \u2192 exactly 9 national digits, +1 \u2192 10)\n   - `AddressNormalizer.normalize` \u2192 trim/collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST/RD/AVE; throws if blank\n   - `PostcodeValidator.validate` \u2192 if postcode present, resolves region from city and enforces NSW 2000\u20132099 / VIC 3000\u20133099 / QLD 4000\u20134099 (UNKNOWN region accepts any)\n\n4. **DailyRegistrationLimit.isReached** \u2014 \u2265 100 owners with today's registration date \u2192 **429 Too Many Requests**\n\n5. **IdentityKey.isDuplicate** \u2014 an existing owner matching on both telephone **and** email \u2192 **409 Conflict**\n\n6. **CityCapacity.isFull** \u2014 \u2265 50 owners already in the same city (case-insensitive) \u2192 **409 Conflict**\n\n## Side-effects (in order)\n\nApplied during mapping (step 3 above, via entity setters):\n- **`setEmail`** stores the email **lower-cased**\n- **`setRegistrationDate`** defaults a missing date to **today** (`LocalDate.now()`) and rolls weekends forward to Monday via `BusinessDay.adjust`\n\nThen in the controller body, after the checks pass:\n\n7. `owner.setNamesakeCount(...)` \u2014 count of existing owners with same first+last name (transient)\n8. `owner.setCustomerCode(...)` \u2014 generates `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (transient)\n9. `owner.setBulkSignupWarning(...)` \u2014 true when > 80 owners share today's date (transient)\n10. `owner.setHouseholdSize(...)` \u2014 count of same-household owners + 1 (transient)\n11. **`clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`** \u2014 the persist, wrapped in `@Transactional`; DB constraint violation \u2192 404\n12. **Audit log line** (`AUDIT.info(...)` \u2014 SLF4J only; no Envers/entity listeners/events/email exist in this path)\n13. Map to `OwnerDto` (computes derived response fields: displayName, initials, householdId, identityKey, membershipNumber/level, locality, contactPreference)\n14. Return **201 Created** with a `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n\n- The handler is **not** `@Transactional`, so `findAllOwners` (read-only) and `saveOwner` run in **separate transactions** \u2014 the duplicate/capacity/limit checks are read outside the write transaction, leaving a TOCTOU race between the check and the save.\n- The entity's own `@NotEmpty`/`@Pattern` constraints on `Owner` are not explicitly invoked here; the DTO-level validation is what runs.\n- The DTO's `sharesHousehold` field is accepted but never used in the create path."
  },
